nding record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 82 that chance alone would give, and <strong>55 record highs</strong>, fewer than the 82 that chance alone would give. The 1910s hold the most record highs of any decade (75). Carbondale's all-time high is 113\u00b0F, on August 9, 1930.","t_chg":"Carbondale's nights have warmed since 1981. Its days cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1981.","p_chg":"Across 105 complete years: Carbondale's average low shows no clear change: \u22120.04\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.13 to +0.06) that includes zero. Carbondale's average high has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.26\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.35 to \u22120.16), about \u22123.2\u00b0F since 1900. July and August highs have edged down across the full record; the 1930s summers were the hottest in it. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1981, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+1.07\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.74 to +1.41) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.51\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.91). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months; October fell. Highs rose in none; 8 months fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Carbondale's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.16 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 44.7 inches a year. The wettest year was 1945 (74.50 in); the driest, 1963 (26.53 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 12 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}